<title>USA: Iowa-S Minn fed cattle trade up $1-$3 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-S Minn fed cattle trade up $1-$3 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slaughter steers and</p>
<p>heifers were up $1.00 to $1.50 on a live basis in a light test</p>
<p>and showed gains of $2.00 to $3.00, dressed, USDA said.</p>
<p>Trade was moderate to active. Demand moderate to good.</p>
<p>Seller interest moderate. Offerings current.</p>
<p>				 Live Sales</p>
<p>Steers: Select to mostly Choice 3-4  1250 lbs few	67.00</p>
<p>Heifers: Select to mostly Choice 2-4 1075-1125 lbs few 65.50</p>
<p>				 Carcass Basis (weight only)</p>
<p>Steers: Select to mostly Choice 2-4 1175-1300 lbs</p>
<p>106.00-107.00 few early 104.00-105.00, few late 107.50.</p>
<p>Holstein: (weight only)</p>
<p>Select to mostly Choice 2-3 1250-1400 lbs  few    101.00</p>
<p>Holsteins: ( grade &amp; weight)</p>
<p>Choice 2-3 1250-1450 lbs			 few    102.00</p>
<p>Select 2-3 1250-1450 lbs				  96.00</p>
<p>Heifers: Select to mostly Choice 2-4 1075-1200 lbs</p>
<p>106.00-107.00</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720))</p>
</text>
